fix(pip): Cover the optic whose lens the engine withheld, and nothing else

Correcting the previous commit, which was too wide. The player narrowed the ghosting to thermal
sights, and that is the precise case the predicate was missing.

StableOverlaysActive() already returns true for any optic whose lens this engine renders
(IsSVPActive()), which is why ordinary magnifying sights never ghosted while panning. A thermal
optic has its lens withheld on purpose (svp_scope_state.h), so IsSVPActive() is false for it and it
fell through to the magnification test, which reads hud_fov_params.x - a number the pack's optics
report at or below 1 (the log line for an M82 carrying a sight reads rtZoom=0.0). Treated as a
stable overlay, its image was reprojected with the scene motion vectors and trailed as a ring that
only exists in movement.

The previous commit instead widened the fallback to "aiming and this weapon has lens data", which
would have covered sights that already work and iron sight cases that the pack handles differently.
This version adds exactly the missing case and leaves everything else as it was: the optic facts say
a lens applies (svp_optic_magnifies, svp_lens_fov) while the engine is not rendering one. Iron sight
aiming carries no lens data and stays excluded.